      "EVORAO:biosafetyRestrictions": "Upon transfection of eukaryotic cells, DNA produces viral proteins lacking functional Gag; does not produce infectious particles.",
      "EVORAO:canBeUsedToProduceGmo": false,
      "EVORAO:iataClassification": "NON DANGEROUS GOODS",
      "EVORAO:identificationTechnique": "restriction digest (Hind III), partial sequencing",
      "EVORAO:clonedNucleicAcid": true,
      "skos:note": "a virus-inactivating frameshift (one nucleotide deletion) is present in the coding sequence of gag: C deletion at position 2101);&nbsp;To&nbsp;show the resistance pattern to&nbsp;antiretroviral drugs&nbsp;caused&nbsp;by the mutations&nbsp;present in this viral clone, use e.g. the&nbsp;„mutations list analysis“ function of the&nbsp;public HIV-Grade site&nbsp;at:&nbsp;www.hiv-grade.de/grade_new/",
      "EVORAO:preparationTechnique": "solid phase column extraction",
      "EVORAO:observedMutations": "The virus genome is derived from pNL-NF (pNL4-3 with shortened cellular flank) (doi.org/10.1016/j.jcv.2006.05.001).\r\nmutations as indicated in the name; backbone is NL-BX.\r\nA unique BamHI site was introduced 5’ of protease (ggagcc2207ggaTcc; A->S in Pol; E->D in Gag) and an XmaI site 3’ of protease (ccagga2589ccCggG). \r\nThe original BamHI site as position 8465 was removed (GGATCC->GGATCA change silent in Env; L->S in Rev).\r\nclone has a C deletion at position 2101 => frameshift in gag, rendering the virus defective!",
